<DocsLayout
  title="niu-git — native Windows Git"
  description="niu-git product page: real git-for-windows C sources built natively with MSVC — no MSYS, no OpenSSL (schannel + the Windows cert store), no bundled shell/perl; git --version in ~14 ms versus Git Bash's 45–103 ms; the shell-scripted parts run on niubash's sh."
  path="/en/products/niu-git/"
  lang="en"
  enPath="/products/niu-git/"
  jsonLdExtra={[productJsonLd, faqJsonLd(productFaq, 'en')]}
  ogImage="/og/niu-git.png"
  zhBanner
>
  <header class="doc-head">
    <h1>niu-git</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Native Windows Git, no MSYS: the real git-for-windows C sources built with MSVC —
      no bundled bash, no bundled perl, no bundled OpenSSL; TLS goes through schannel and the
      Windows certificate store. The <code>git</code> on PATH is git itself, <code>git --version</code>
      starts in about 14 ms, and the scripted parts (hooks, bisect, mergetool) run on niubash's
      <code>sh</code>.
    </p>
    <div class="badges">
      <span class="p-badge">C (MSVC)</span>
      <span class="p-badge">Windows</span>
      <span class="p-badge">stable</span>
    </div>
    <p class="meta-line">
      <a href="https://github.com/unixwin/niu-git" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/unixwin/niu-git ↗</a>
      <span class="dot">·</span> Star 0
      <span class="dot">·</span> latest v2.56.0.1 (repo-meta, measured 2026-10-19; no releases page — the tag is the version)
    </p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2 id="why">Why niu-git</h2>
    <p>
      Nearly everyone on Windows has a git on PATH that "boots an MSYS2 runtime before doing work":
      calling from cmd / PowerShell hops through the cmd\git.exe launcher, calling from Git Bash pays
      an extra fork — so every git status pays tax for a POSIX world you don't need. niu-git's stance
      is plain: the git binary is a C program, so build it natively as one; git's scripted parts are
      shell, so hand them to a real shell.
    </p>
    <details class="zh-fold">
      <summary>中文原文 · Chinese original（4 张卡片全文）</summary>
      <div lang="zh-CN">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>快是结构性的，不是调优</strong>——Git Bash 的 git 跑在 MSYS2 运行时里，每次调用都付一遍 POSIX 运行时初始化；niu-git 的 usr\bin\git.exe 就是 git 本体：一次 CreateProcess，无 MSYS DLL、进程树里无 bash 无 perl。</li>
          <li><strong>无 MSYS、无 OpenSSL、无捆绑脚本运行时</strong>——MSVC + CMake 构建 git-for-windows 真实 C 源码；TLS 只走 schannel；zlib / iconv 静态链接；shell 脚本部分由 PATH 上的 niubash sh 承担。</li>
          <li><strong>参数保真：引号纪律与消息字面字节</strong>——commit -m 载荷、D:\dir\ 路径规格、CJK 与多行消息逐字节存活；差分套件 49/49 钉死；消息载荷永不改写。</li>
          <li><strong>边界诚实：不带的说清楚</strong>——perl 命令（send-email、svn、cvs*）不提供而不是运行时才失败；git-gui / gitk 不随发；git grep -P 没有——用 WinuxCmd 的 grep -P。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="features">Core features</h2>
    <p>
      Real git C sources, natively built with MSVC; ~14 ms startup; schannel TLS with credential
      helpers untouched; a clean division of labor with niubash's sh; an upstream test baseline on
      record; and it arrives together with niubash. Full six-point list (Chinese):
    </p>
    <details class="zh-fold">
      <summary>中文原文 · Chinese original（六条特性全文）</summary>
      <div lang="zh-CN">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>真 git C 源码，MSVC 原生构建</strong>——上游 git-for-windows 的 C 源码 + 仓内三枚补丁（#1 schannel 容忍 stale http.sslBackend；#2 POSIX 形路径参数 + 消息守卫；#3 system prefix 自定位），源码永不入仓，CI 拉上游 tarball 打补丁。</li>
          <li><strong>~14 ms 启动</strong>——wpm flat 布局实测 git --version 13.7 ms 均值；v2.55.0.5 起根入口 launcher 退役，无包装 hop。</li>
          <li><strong>schannel TLS 与凭据不越权</strong>——TLS 走 Windows 证书库；自配的任何凭据 helper 照常生效；系统 gitconfig 刻意不设默认 helper；自带 172 KB 的 wincred 小助手。</li>
          <li><strong>与 niubash sh 的分工</strong>——hooks、git bisect、git mergetool、git filter-branch、git submodule、git request-pull 跑在 niubash 提供的 sh 上。</li>
          <li><strong>上游测试基线在案</strong>——curated subset 2861 ok / 14 例 # TODO known breakage / 0 硬失败；t0001-init 102/103。</li>
          <li><strong>随 niubash 一起到货</strong>——niubash 1.4.0 的 Windows 发行包经 wpm 预装 niu-git（ARM64 同样预装）。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="install">Install &amp; quick start</h2>
    <p>
      Windows: the niubash release package already preloads niu-git (the bundle list lives in
      niubash's scripts/release/preinstall.json; niu-git and gawk are windows-x64 assets, the ARM64
      leg ships only ripgrep and fd per the preinstall.json notes). Verify:
    </p>
    <div class="cmd">
      <pre><code>{verifyGit}</code></pre>
      <CopyButton copy={verifyGit} label="Copy" title="Copy to clipboard" />
    </div>
    <p>Migrating from a MinGit shim install (the flat layout needs WinuxCmd/wpm 1.1.9+):</p>
    <div class="cmd">
      <pre><code>{migrateBoth}</code></pre>
      <CopyButton copy={migrateBoth} label="Copy" title="Copy to clipboard" />
    </div>
    <p class="first-run">
      One-line first-run check: <code>git --version</code> should print a version string of the
      <code>2.56.0.windows.2.niugit</code> shape — upstream suffix and the niu-git distro marker both
      present. niubash users can skip this: the Windows package already ships niu-git (x64 and ARM64).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="deep">Deep dive: speed, the native toolchain and sh interplay</h2>
    <h3>Speed comparison</h3>
    <p>
      Windows x64, warm cache, Python subprocess timing, 15 rounds, a small repo (measured 2026-10).
      The gap is structural: niu-git reaches the git binary in one CreateProcess; the Git Bash side
      pays MSYS2 runtime initialization per call (plus a fork inside the prompt).
    </p>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="cli-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>git on PATH</th><th>git --version</th><th>git status --porcelain</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            speed.map((r) => (
              <tr class={r.best ? 'is-best' : ''}>
                <td>{r.best ? <strong>{r.who}</strong> : r.who}</td>
                <td>{r.version}</td>
                <td>{r.status}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <details class="zh-fold">
      <summary>中文原文 · Chinese original（MSVC / schannel 与 sh 联动 两节全文）</summary>
      <div lang="zh-CN">
        <p><strong>MSVC / schannel：原生工具链到底</strong>——构建链是 MSVC + CMake（+ vcpkg），TLS 只编 schannel：证书与系统更新走 Windows 证书库，不携带 OpenSSL 及其随附 dll；zlib 与 iconv 静态链接。patch #1 容忍遗留的 http.sslBackend 配置——警告并回落，而不是拒绝启动。</p>
        <p><strong>与 niubash sh 联动</strong>——git 的脚本面不是被删掉，是被分工：hooks、git bisect、git mergetool、git filter-branch、git submodule、git request-pull 交给 PATH 上的 sh（即 <a href="/en/products/niubash/">niubash</a> 的 sh shim）。perl 依赖的 send-email / svn / cvs* 诚实缺席；git grep -P 没有时用 <a href="/en/products/winuxcmd/">WinuxCmd</a> 的 grep -P。路径方言总账见 <a href="/en/docs/paths-and-msys/">路径与 MSYS</a>。</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="bench">Measured numbers</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="cli-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Metric</th><th>niu-git</th><th>Contrast</th><th>Source</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            bench.map((r) => (
              <tr>
                <td>{r.a}</td>
                <td><strong>{r.b}</strong></td>
                <td>{r.c}</td>
                <td><span class="src">{r.src}</span></td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="news">Release feed</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="cli-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Version</th><th>Date</th><th>Summary</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            news.map((n) => (
              <tr>
                <td><code>{n.version}</code></td>
                <td>{n.date}</td>
                <td>{n.summary}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="src-line">
      niu-git is outside changelogs.json's fetch scope (no releases page, no CHANGELOG — the tag is
      the version, per the FACTS.json products ruling); the table above summarizes the in-repo README,
      wpm/niugit.json and portal repo-meta tag measurements. Other repos' full feed:
      <a href="/en/changelog/">changelog</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="links">Related links</h2>
    <h3>On this site</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/en/products/niubash/">niubash product page</a> — the other half of the sh interplay; the Windows package ships niu-git</li>
      <li><a href="/en/products/winuxcmd/">WinuxCmd product page</a> — the provider of wpm and grep -P</li>
      <li><a href="/en/docs/paths-and-msys/">Paths &amp; MSYS</a> · <a href="/en/benchmarks/">Benchmarks</a> (git startup ~14 ms vs 45–103 ms) · <a href="/en/changelog/">Changelog</a></li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Off site</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/unixwin/niu-git" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub repo ↗</a> (a patch repo: sources never committed; CI pulls the upstream tarball and applies patches/)</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/unixwin/niu-git/tags" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tags (versions are tags) ↗</a></li>
      <li><a href="/products/niu-git/" hreflang="zh-CN" lang="zh-CN">Chinese edition of this page</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <FaqSection items={productFaq} lang="en" />
</DocsLayout>

